  "content": "<p>« <a href=\"../../../pages/positive-definite-matrices-and-applications/exam-3-review/index.html\">Previous</a> | <a href=\"../../../pages/final-course-review/index.html\">Next</a> »</p>\n\n    <h3 id=\"session-overview\">Session Overview</h3>\n\n<p><table>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td>\n\n<img src=\"../../../static_resources/33cadc81b4b388da0a111af7336a2561_Exam_3.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n</td>\n\n<td>\n</p>\n<p>This exam starts with a question about singular values. They all equal 1 when A<sup>T</sup>A = I. Question 2 in the exam uses eigenvalues and eigenvectors to compute powers of A: diagonalize first! </p>\n</td>\n\n</tr>\n\n</table>\n\n\n    <h3 id=\"check-yourself\">Check Yourself</h3>\n\n\n    <h4 id=\"exams-and-solutions\">Exams and Solutions</h4>\n\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"../../../resources/mit18_06scf11_ex3/index.html\">Exams (PDF)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"../../../resources/mit18_06scf11_ex3s/index.html\">Solutions (PDF)</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>« <a href=\"../../../pages/positive-definite-matrices-and-applications/exam-3-review/index.html\">Previous</a> | <a href=\"../../../pages/final-course-review/index.html\">Next</a> »</p>\n",
